Ray,

Did you upgrade your version of Access?  I seem to recall that if the
product was upgraded, it installed Real-Mode software; on the other hand, if
it was a fresh install, only '286-mode code was used.

The solution, if I remember correctly, was to rename or delete one of the
binaries so that Access would think it was a fresh install and wouldn't load
the '386 code.

I don't make this stuff up -- the truth is stranger than fiction...

