mapping CISC instructions onto RISC - one of the advantages of RISC
is that there are (relatively) few instructions each of which is very
fast - whereas CISC is a bunch of slower instructions that do a lot.
The mapping is usually not very positive for the RISC station.  On most
of the apps we tried (sorry 0 too long ago to remember which) the Alpha
seemed to run at about 286-386 speeds at best.  

This comparison makes the common abstraction layer at the lowest
possible level - the x86 hardware - putting the Alpha at a disadvantage.
If NT moves that abstraction level high enough, it could work and
perform reasonably.

andy
