Subject: Printer Drivers

There seems to be some problems with loading both Alpha and Intel print 
drivers on the same system so that any platform can attach without the 
drivers loaded locally.

If someone who is good at writing instructions could re-write these we 
could add it to a FAQ.

Thanks

----------------------------------------------------------------------
To load a I386 print driver on an Alpha server:

Scenario 1 (NT 3.51):
(assumes PRINTER.INF exists in expanded form on CD-ROM E:\I386)
In PrintManager select properties for the printer in question.
Under Printer Type select Other
For path enter E:\I386
Select printer from list and accept.

Scenario 2 (NT 3.5):
(if PRINTER.INF is compressed you need to expand it)
Expand PRINTER.IN_  by typing:
    EXPAND  E:\I386\PRINTER.IN_  C:\USERS\DEFAULT\PRINTER.INF
In PrintManager select properties for the printer in question.
Undr Printer Type select Other
For path enter C:\USERS\DEFAULT
 - you will get a new box with a new path and a list of printers.
Highlight printer from list and now enter E:\I386 for path and accept.

