From: Aaron Sakovich <aaron@garply.com>
Subject: Re: FWD: Printer Drivers

At 08:58 AM 10/5/95 EDT, Michael H. Spence, Eastman Chemical wrote:
>If you load the i386 drivers onto the Alpha server when creating the printer
>queue and sharing it out, will this effect the Windows 3.1 users that 
>attach to the printer queue?  

No, that's one of the differences between NT and Windows.  An NT server
houses the drivers for other NT machines.  Windows only houses the drivers
for itself.  So when you print from a Windows machine to a printer via an NT
server, the driver used is the one loaded on the Windows machine.
Conversely, if you print from one NT machine via another, the other thread
about setting up print drivers on NT comes into play.

