clarifications on 32/64/128/256 bits and Alpha uProcessors:

 Alpha instruction is represented by 32 bits. So a dual issue Alpha uProcessor
 like the 21064 family or the 21066 family, fetches two, 32 bits, instruction
 per cycle (at peak performance), while a quad issue Alpha uProcessor (21164
 is the only one available now) fetches four, 32 bits, instructions/cycle, at
 peak performance.

 data path - The 21066 is limited to 64 bits datapath. The 21064/21064A can
 operate at 64 bits or 128 bits. It is up to the designer of the system to
 choose between the 64 and 128. From the uProcessor point of view this is done
 at initialization time. The 21164 has 128 bits data path.

 Digital manufactures and sells Alpha based systems that have either 64 or
 128 bits data paths (from the Processor). The 64 bit data path is not unique
 to the Alpha-XL family and the are other Alpha based system that uses 64 bits
 data path

Meir Licht - Digital Equipment Corporation
          

