Message-ID: <199510180932.KAA11923@vbormc.vbo.dec.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Oct 95 10:32:46 MET
From: Gordon McNab <gordon@ayjen1.enet.dec.com>
Subject: RE: AXP 1000: NT installation fails

Lambert,

>I know that I've seen this message before: it has something to do
>with the driver for the Cirrus Video adapter. I remenber something
>like copying the driver from CD to floppy, but I don't know
>what to do exactly.

Copy the files from:

<cdrom>:\alpha\drvlib\video\alpha\cirrus

to a floppy and restart the Windows NT Installation. Perform a
Custom setup and change the type of video card when presented
with a menu about your computers configuration. 

Choose 'Other (requires disk from manufacturer)' and install the 
driver from the floppy disk.

Gordon

