Subject: AXP 1000: NT installation fails : the answer

Hello,

I've asked a question on installing WNT on a Alphaserver 1000.
The answer is (as always) simple, as i found out after trying:

When installing, a screen is presented with the hardware
options, like keyboard, mouse, and the graphical adapter. Move the
cursor to the adapter you want to change (the VGA adapter) and
press "enter". Change the VGA adapter to other, and you are asked
for a floppy with the driver.

The floppy can be created from the WNT CD-ROM, but also by putting
the driver on a DOS formatted floppy. The files you want are on the
Digital ftp server. Copy all the files to floppy.
( http://ftp.digital.com:80/pub/Digital/Alpha/systems/as1000/nt/video_adapters/cirrus )

I hope this will help someone in the future, I'll try some more next
time before polluting this mailing list  :-)

