From tsharma@dialcall.com Tue Oct 24 09:16:08 1995 CDT
Message-ID: <308CF623@alcnwgw1>
Date: Tue, 24 Oct 95 10:12:00 EDT
From: Sharma, Tushar <tsharma@dialcall.com>
Subject: RE: ntfs the same old story

Stefano,

     I do not have any direct experience with an Alphaserver 400, but I have 
a
DECpc150 at home (on firmware version 1.9). Here is how I have installed WNT 
3.51.

mb
partition which will ALWAYS be FAT and cannot be converted to NTFS. This 
will also
be your C: drive which has the OS loader stuff in it. (Do NOT install WNT in 
this partition). I think arcinst will let you set up more than one partition 
on your hard drive.
I can see all partition(s) thru an option named 'display hardware 
configuration' in my ARC console.

Now from the ARC console menu, choose 'set up the system' (I am not sure 
about this, your hardware documentation should help here). Find an option 
which says
'Install Windows NT from CD-ROM' and go thru the setup.

If let us say you have a 1000 mb drive, and 10mb has gone to this FAT 
partition, you
are left with 990mb which is the partition where you can install WNT. After 
you go thru setup the machine should reboot and run OS loader and then run a 
'convert' for you and convert the 990 mb partition(or whatever your 
partition is) to NTFS. The 10 mb
partition will NEVER be converted to a NTFS partition.

I think your problem is that WNT is being installed in the same partition as 
the OS loader stuff is and this can not be converted to NTFS. I hope this 
helps.

.Tushar.

